@EMPLOYEE_MANAGEMENTAPII_HostAddress = http://localhost:5064

### 1. Get all employees
GET {{EMPLOYEE_MANAGEMENTAPII_HostAddress}}/api/employees
Accept: application/json

### 2. Search employees (e.g. search 'Alice')
GET {{EMPLOYEE_MANAGEMENTAPII_HostAddress}}/api/employees?search=Alice
Accept: application/json

### 3. Filter by department
GET {{EMPLOYEE_MANAGEMENTAPII_HostAddress}}/api/employees?department=Engineering
Accept: application/json

### 4. Get employee by ID
GET {{EMPLOYEE_MANAGEMENTAPII_HostAddress}}/api/employees/1
Accept: application/json

### 5. Create a new employee
POST {{EMPLOYEE_MANAGEMENTAPII_HostAddress}}/api/employees
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "John",
  "lastName": "Doe",
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "department": "Engineering",
  "position": "Software Engineer",
  "salary": 85000,
  "hireDate": "2024-01-15"
}

### 6. Update an employee
PUT {{EMPLOYEE_MANAGEMENTAPII_HostAddress}}/api/employees/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Alice",
  "lastName": "Johnson",
  "email": "alice.johnson@example.com",
  "department": "Engineering",
  "position": "Lead Software Engineer",
  "salary": 105000,
  "hireDate": "2022-03-15"
}

### 7. Delete an employee
DELETE {{EMPLOYEE_MANAGEMENTAPII_HostAddress}}/api/employees/5
